# Authoring sources, which are not what ships.
#
# A `.blend` is ten times the size of the `.gltf` it exports and changes on
# every save; committing one would put a binary nobody can diff into the history
# of a repository whose asset budget is 24 MB. The *export* is committed, under
# `assets/`, and `pnpm assets:build` compresses it from there. Keep the
# originals somewhere they are backed up — just not here. See docs/assets.md §8.
*.blend
*.blend[0-9]
*.psd
*.xcf
*.substance
*.sbs
*.sbsar
*.wav
*.aif
*.aiff
*.flac

# Written and deleted again by `pnpm run guardrails`. Ignored so that a probe
# surviving a crashed run can never be committed. ESLint and tsc still see it —
# neither reads .gitignore — which is the whole point of the file.
**/__guardrail_probe__.ts
__guardrail_lock__.yaml

# Recorded matches (`pnpm demo`, and a server run with GLADIATOR_DEMO_DIR set).
# A demo is a debugging artifact about one session — the useful one is always
# the one somebody just produced, and the format has a version in it so an old
# file is refused rather than misread. `tools/demo.ts`.
demos/
